From: SR2 Launcher <sr2-launcher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] app: SR2 Launcher name, memory defaults and build stamp
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Info.plist: the app is called SR2 Launcher on the Home Screen.
- SR2Launcher.seedDefaults (MadeiraConfig.swift), first in MadeiraApp.init:
  once per install, on a device under 10 GB, writes the memory settings
  Slime Rancher 2's world loaded with (swap-mb = 4096,
  env.MADEIRA_SWAP_COVERAGE = wide, donor-pool-mb = 2048), each only where
  madeira.cfg has no value for it.
- The Setup Guide's About names this as a modified version of Madeira 0.2.0
  and where its source is.
- package-ipa.sh builds with ENABLE_DEBUG_DYLIB=NO and refuses a
  Madeira.debug.dylib: the app's code goes in the Madeira executable, as in
  Madeira's 0.2.0 release ("ml989: running image .../Madeira"). With Xcode's
  Debug default (code in Madeira.debug.dylib behind a stub) build 3 died on
  the phone as Wine connected to its server, before the launcher's own code
  ran. runtime-components.py ipa accepts either layout.
- package-ipa.sh: MADEIRA_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER overrides the project's bundle
  identifier for the app and both extensions; Info.plist gets MadeiraBuild
  (MADEIRA_BUILD_STAMP, else "0.2.0 · SR2 Launcher 1 · <UTC time>"), which
  the [build] log line and Get Help show.
